# Autoconf inputs and shell scripts must keep LF line endings on every platform.
#
# `R CMD check` reads configure, configure.in, configure.ac and cleanup byte by
# byte and fails them on any CR:
#
#   Found the following shell script(s) with CR or CRLF line endings:
#         configure.ac
#   Non-Windows OSes require LF line endings.
#
# The files are LF in this repository, but a checkout on a Windows runner (where
# git sets core.autocrlf=true system-wide) converts them on the way out of git,
# so the tarball built there carries CRLF. Pinning eol=lf keeps the checkout LF
# regardless of the platform's core.autocrlf setting.
configure       text eol=lf
configure.ac    text eol=lf
configure.in    text eol=lf
configure.win   text eol=lf
cleanup         text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
